                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_32\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds a 6th \"left\" entry to the column-alignment array used for the\nnon-timetable branch of the instructor's class-assignment table in\nInstructorDetailAction.java:\n\n    new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\"},\n -> new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\", \"left\"},\n\nThis array is paired with a header-labels array that has 6 entries\n(MSG.columnClass(), MSG.columnInstructorCheckConflicts(), MSG.columnInstructorShare(),\nMSG.columnTeachingResponsibility(), MSG.columnLimit(), MSG.columnManager()) and a\nWebTable declared with column count 6. Because the alignment array only had 5\nentries while the table expected 6 columns, WebTable threw an\nArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException whenever an instructor had class assignments but no\ncommitted timetable yet (issue #27).\n\nCandidate_32 is where this mismatch was introduced. In this commit, the\n\"no timetable\" WebTable was changed from 5 to 6 columns: the column count changed\nfrom `new WebTable(5, ...)` to `new WebTable(6, ...)`, and MSG.columnTeachingResponsibility()\nwas added to the header-labels array (making it 6 elements). However, the\nalignment array `new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\"}` was left\nunchanged at 5 elements. This is precisely the pattern (extra header/column count\nwithout a corresponding alignment entry) that the fix commit corrects by appending\nthe missing 6th \"left\".\n\nEarlier candidates (e.g. candidate_26) show the header and alignment arrays for\nthis branch both correctly sized at 5 elements, confirming the mismatch did not\nexist before candidate_32. No later candidate before the fix modifies this specific\nalignment array, so candidate_32 is the first and only commit introducing the bug.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
